  "report": "This patient has triple-negative breast cancer, which is associated with higher pCR rates. However, the tumour is large and shows low-to-moderate enhancement kinetics in both core and rim regions, suggesting poor vascular permeability and perfusion. These imaging features, combined with the large volume, are concerning for lower likelihood of pCR. The MammaPrint status is not high-risk, but does not strongly support pCR. Overall, the evidence points to an unlikely pCR."
}

